"Print the path of the [store derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-"
"derivation) produced by `nixpkgs#hello`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-path-info.md:91
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-path-info.md:93
msgid ""
"This command shows information about the store paths produced by "
"[_installables_](./nix.md#installables), or about all paths in the store if "
"you pass `--all`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-path-info.md:96
msgid ""
"By default, this command only prints the store paths. You can get additional "
"information by passing flags such as `--closure-size`, `--size`, `--sigs` or "
"`--json`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-path-info.md:99
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-path-info.md:101
msgid ""
"Note that `nix path-info` does not build or substitute the _installables_ "
"you specify. Thus, if the corresponding store paths don't already exist, "
"this command will fail. You can use `nix build` to ensure that they exist."
msgstr ""

